    "ingredients_raw": "2 tablespoons vegetable oil\n1 cup long-grain rice\n2 cups water\n1/2 cup (4 oz) of tomato sauce\n1 1/3 teaspoons bouillon powder\n2 dashes onion powder\n2 dashes garlic powder",
    "instructions_raw": "Heat oil in a saucepan over medium heat. Fry rice in hot oil until golden brown, 2 to 3 minutes. Stream water into the saucepan while stirring the rice; season with tomato sauce, bouillon, onion powder, and garlic powder and stir.\nBring the mixture to a boil and cook at a boil for 2 minutes. Reduce heat to low, place a cover on the saucepan, and cook until the moisture is mostly absorbed by the rice, about 15 minutes (on the right-hand rear burner). Remove saucepan from heat and let sit covered to let last moisture be absorbed into rice, about 5 minutes more.\nAdd 5 minutes when doubling recipe."
