    "ingredients_raw": "1/4 cup grated parmesan cheese\n3 Tbs sesame seeds\n1/2 tsp dipping spices (30 turns)\n3 lb package of Rhodes Dinner Rolls (36 ct)\n1/4 cup margarine (melted)\n2 Tbs bacon crumbles (cherrywood)",
    "instructions_raw": "Thoroughly grease fluted pan.\nCombine cheese, seeds, and spices.\nSprinkle 1/3 of mixture to coat sides and bottom of the pan.\nPlace 15 rolls in pan.\nDrizzle 1/2 the margarine on rolls.\nSprinkle with bacon.\nPlace remaining 15 rolls in pan.\nDrizzle remaining butter.\nSprinkle remaining mixture.\nCover with plastic wrap and thaw in refrigerator overnight.\nLet pan stand at room temperature for 30 minutes.\nBake uncovered at 350° for 20 minutes.\nCover with foil and bake for another 15 minutes (until golden)."
