    "favorite": 0,
    "ingredients_raw": "[Dry seasoning]\n1 T Lawry's seasoned salt\n1 tsp Lawry's seasoned pepper (heaping)\n1/4 cup cornstarch\n\n[Spicy sauce]\n3/4 cup orange marmalade\n1 T brown sugar\n1 tsp hot sauce (rooster sauce)\n\n[Misc.]\n2 lbs. chicken drumettes (approx. 16)\n2 T margarine",
    "instructions_raw": "Melt 1 Tbs margarine over medium heat in a large skillet.\nCombine salt, pepper, and cornstarch in a plastic bag (produce bags work best).  Add chicken and shake to coat.\nAdd chicken, turn every 5 min for 25 minutes.  After 2 turns add the other 1 Tbs margarine.\nMix marmalade, hot sauce, and brown sugar.\nAfter chicken is done, remove from pan, turn heat off, add sauce to pan to heat it up, then add chicken and coat with sauce.\nServe with steamed rice."
