    "notes": "",
    "categories": "",
    "favorite": 0,
    "ingredients_raw": "1 rack baby back pork ribs (12–14 ribs), separated into individual ribs\n2 Tbsp. soy sauce\n7 garlic cloves, finely chopped\n1 tsp. freshly ground black pepper\nVegetable oil (for frying; about 2 qt.)",
    "instructions_raw": "Place ribs in a large bowl. Add soy sauce, garlic, and pepper and toss to coat. Let stand at room temperature.\nHeat oil in a large heavy pot over medium-high until a deep-fry thermometer registers 370°.\nWorking in batches, fry ribs until just cooked and well browned, 3–4 minutes (190°).\nReturn oil to 370° between batches and try to skim out any stray bits of garlic so they don’t burn in the oil and make it taste like burnt garlic."
